# Work history - revision, identity and recovery
date: 2026-10-31
who: Codex Prime
state: N4NN development material; proposed requirements and findings, not seated law

## Why preserve this understanding
The grok.com prototype gave us a concrete way to examine preservation. Its task
revision and review-binding failures reveal distinctions the app must keep explicit.
Source: 0523/05.01 full Prime review and its evidence, reviewed commit
e94ca6985789c503e3d4f37019042068eef6e8f4. The old wording disappearing and stale
return becoming fresh were reproduced with explicit in-memory platform substitutes;
these are qualified serial unit probes, not native Windows or concurrency proof.

## Idea 1 - selected state backed by recoverable history
A current task cannot be represented only by an overwritten file plus its old
hash. A hash identifies lost content but cannot reconstruct it. Before selecting
a replacement, preserve exact old task AND face bytes, why it changed, authorizing
task/request reference, before/after identities and the selection transition.
Do not invent authorization retrospectively. An explanation must land with the
work, with an exact reference to the instruction that permits the change.
An interrupted revision must expose incomplete work or leave the prior selection
usable. It must not claim a complete new state while the old one is unrecoverable.
Retention layout/schema is still a design choice; no new face assignment is made.

## Idea 2 - distinguish address, material revision and write token
Address says which work and pass. A task/revision binding says which material,
agreement and evidence a worker or reviewer received. A file hash/write token
guards the particular physical write. These should not be collapsed.
Mechanical review/pointer construction should not invalidate an otherwise current
judgment. A changed task, origin, relevant evidence or agreement should. Equal
text at two different addresses must not silently become the same task identity.
Keep exact selected source identities; do not choose highest version by filename.
Related local work: 0519/05.01, 0520/05.01, 0522 reviews and integration assignments.

## Idea 3 - historical evidence remains valid without being current
A receipt may still verify perfectly while its return answers an older task.
Preserve and show it as historical/stale. Do not recompute a new review hash against
it and call that implicit reconciliation with a different assignment. A material
change requires an explicit relationship and intelligent judgment within authority.
Keep custody-valid, answers-current-task, review-current and accepted/approved
separate. Stale source/release/claim must not disappear beneath a fresh-looking
next action. An honest hold can be more useful than a misleading completed state.

## Idea 4 - interruption and refusal are preserved work states
Temporary files, copy progress and incomplete transitions carry evidence. A later
operation must not truncate or replace the only partial record silently. Recovery
checks actual source/destination identities and records what it resumes or refuses.
If it cannot proceed, retain what happened and say exactly what is missing.
Smallest acceptance examples: recover prior wording after revision; observe a
partial revision after interruption; reject an old return as current for a new task;
recover an unresolved question after restart; inspect why each result occurred.

## Idea 5 - platform assumptions belong in the operating contract
The Linux prototype could not run its write loop on this Windows desk: fcntl was
unavailable and low-level text-mode writes altered bytes. Record supported OS and
runtime, exact byte behavior, tested capabilities and untested limits. This is a
dependency/contract question, not a reason to claim every model output is unsafe.
If an expected environment is unavailable, report a checkpoint with the smallest
needed input; do not quietly substitute a platform and claim target validation.

## Boundaries and next use
These are design lessons worth retaining before the next 05, not a demand for
a universal version store or logging service. Reuse current custody/history where
it can supply the contract. Do not rewrite old captures, migrate addresses or change
active source code from this page. See 0417/06.01 for correct return routing and
0416/01.003 for inspectability and careful compute rejection.
